     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of 850 mg to 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg** three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg** twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg** three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf you confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, I'll need that stated explicitly, and I'd suggest a pharmacist review it. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
